    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8913954a-abf2-5cba-a2f3-cdac64ea6f71",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -31 & 50 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{31}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 27 \\\\ 8 & -7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-8R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -31 & 50 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-8R_{3}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
